m. |\n| IF-306 | row | new | stdout consumer seam for per-invocation outcomes. | Separates command output from arguments and exit status. |\n| IF-307 | row | new | exit-code consumer seam for 0/1/2 outcomes. | Separates result status from arguments and stdout. |\n| TC-388 | method, expected | Stop/later-message finality only. | Adds absent, stale, and timely finish-notice cases. | Verifies LLR-347’s settled finality rule. |\n| TC-391 | verifies | included IF-305 | adds IF-306 | It observes stdout outcomes as well as CLI selection. |\n| TC-394 | verifies | included IF-305 | adds IF-307 | It observes the no-session and absent-session exit outcomes. |\n| id-watermark | IF | `305` | `307` | Allocated IF-306 and IF-307 once through `trace.py --bump-ids`. |\n\nPerspective record created at [plan.perspectives.toml](C:\\Projects\\ai-template.wt\\wi-961\\docs\\plans\\WI-961\\plan.perspectives.toml). Its strict check reports: `no findings`.\n\nBuilder-list reconciliation:\n\n1. Confirmed: LLR-347’s reader result symbols are present and claimed.\n2. Confirmed: LLR-351 claims the service-result constant in both modules.\n3. Confirmed and amended: IF-245 now names the constant.\n4. Confirmed: TC-387 includes the CLI-result witness.\n5. Extended: LLR-351 now explicitly excludes own invocation contributions from service-record classification.\n6. Refuted as a current carrier: session-protocol does not realize completion ingestion; removed from LLR-356.\n7. Confirmed and amended: D-007 finish-notice finality is reflected in LLR-347 and TC-388.\n8. Confirmed and amended: SR-244 now has the correct bounded domain, hand-back rationale, and retry/resume distinction.\n9. Confirmed: IF-245 notes already accurately covered transcript/meta reads.\n10. Confirmed and amended: IF-245 names `claude_home` and `transcript_time`.\n11. Confirmed and amended: IF-246 names `CALL_LOG_RE`.\n\nChecks:\n\n- `trace.py --bump-ids` — `IF 305 -> 307`.\n- `trace.py --strict` — `orphans=0 integrity=0`, with e